{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SerialExecutor"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"text":"Executor","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Executor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScF","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Custom Actor Executors","type":"heading","anchor":"Custom-Actor-Executors","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, all actor types execute tasks on a shared global concurrent pool."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The global pool does not guarantee any thread (or dispatch queue) affinity,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so actors are free to use different threads as they execute tasks.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The runtime may perform various optimizations to minimize un-necessary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread switching."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sometimes it is important to be able to customize the execution behavior","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of an actor. For example, when an actor is known to perform heavy blocking","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operations (such as IO), and we would like to keep this work ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"off"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the global","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shared pool, as blocking it may prevent other actors from being responsive.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can implement a custom executor, by conforming a type to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, and implementing the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"enqueue(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once implemented, you can configure an actor to use such executor by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implementing the actor’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Actor\/unownedExecutor"},{"type":"text","text":" computed property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you could accept an executor in the actor’s initializer,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store it as a variable (in order to retain it for the duration of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"actor’s lifetime), and return it from the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unownedExecutor"},{"type":"text","text":" computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property like this:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["actor MyActor {","  let myExecutor: MyExecutor","","  \/\/ accepts an executor to run this actor on.","  init(executor: MyExecutor) {","    self.myExecutor = executor","  }","","  nonisolated var unownedExecutor: UnownedSerialExecutor {","    self.myExecutor.asUnownedSerialExecutor()","  }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is also possible to use a form of shared executor, either created as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"global or static property, which you can then re-use for every MyActor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["actor MyActor {","  \/\/ Serial executor reused by *all* instances of MyActor!","  static let sharedMyActorsExecutor = MyExecutor() \/\/ implements SerialExecutor","","","  nonisolated var unownedExecutor: UnownedSerialExecutor {","    Self.sharedMyActorsExecutor.asUnownedSerialExecutor()","  }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the example above, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all"}]},{"type":"text","text":" “MyActor” instances would be using the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serial executor, which would result in only one of such actors ever being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run at the same time. This may be useful if some of your code has some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“specific thread” requirement when interoperating with non-Swift runtimes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for example."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Since the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnownedSerialExecutor"},{"text":" returned by the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unownedExecutor"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does not","type":"text"}]},{"text":" retain the executor, you must make sure the lifetime of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it extends beyond the lifetime of any actor or task using it, as otherwise","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it may attempt to enqueue work on a released executor object, causing a crash.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The executor returned by unownedExecutor ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"must","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" always be the same object,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and returning different executors can lead to unexpected behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, you can also use existing serial executor implementations,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as Dispatch’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSerialQueue"},{"type":"text","text":" or others."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Executors","anchor":"Executors","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Executor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ExecutorJob","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskExecutor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/PartialAsyncTask","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnownedJob","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/JobPriority","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnownedSerialExecutor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnownedTaskExecutor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SchedulingExecutor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/globalConcurrentExecutor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withTaskExecutorPreference(_:isolation:operation:)"],"generated":true}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A service that executes jobs."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Executor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sendable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SendableMetatype"],"type":"inheritsFrom"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Swift","relatedModules":[]}],"platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"8.0"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"8.0"},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false,